    <section class="af__step" :class="isOn(3) ? 'is-on' : ''">
      <div class="af__head">
        <h2>Ticket appearance</h2>
        <p>Leave this alone and tickets look exactly as they do now. Change anything and only
          this event's tickets change.</p>
      </div>

    {# ── THE TICKET'S APPEARANCE ─────────────────────────────────────────────
       Per event, not per site: this platform runs an awards ceremony, a summit and a
       training day in the same year, and they do not share a look. A site-wide ticket
       theme would mean every event after the first wears somebody else's clothes.

       The preview is live but it is a PREVIEW — the real ticket is rendered by
       templates/pages/events/ticket.twig from values EventTicketDesign has validated. The
       colour is the one field here whose value ends up inside a `style` attribute, so it is
       refused rather than escaped on save AND again on render.

       `x-data` sits on a wrapper with no static `style`, and every bound style below is on
       a tag that has none of its own — AlpineStyleClobberTest fails the build otherwise. #}
    {% if design_missing is not empty %}
      <div style="border:1px solid #ecd9a0;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin-top:6px;background:#fffdf5">
        <strong style="font-size:14px">Ticket design needs one more step</strong>
        <p style="font-size:13px;color:#6b5312;margin:6px 0 0;line-height:1.7">
          These columns are not in the database yet:
          <code>{{ design_missing|join('</code>, <code>')|raw }}</code>. Run
          <strong>/__setup/migrate</strong> and this section appears. Until then tickets use
          the standard design, which is exactly what they did before.
        </p>
      </div>
    {% else %}
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--cn-line-card);border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin-top:6px;background:#fafcfa"
         {# `imageField` is the RAW column and `image` is the resolved one. The address box is
            bound to the raw value on purpose: seeded with the resolved one, opening any event
            with a cover photo and pressing Save copied the cover into `ticket_image` — after
            which changing the cover no longer changed the ticket, and nothing said why. #}
         x-data="tkDesign({{ {
            accent: design.accent,
            theme: design.theme,
            note: design.note,
            image: design.image,
            imageField: row.ticket_image|default(''),
            title: row.title|default('Your event'),
            when: row.event_date|default(''),
            venue: row.venue|default(''),
            showQr: design.show_qr,
            art: { src: artwork_src|default(''), edit: artwork_edit|default({}),
                   ratio: artwork_ratio|default(1.5), on: artwork_missing is empty }
         }|json_encode }})">
      <input type="hidden" name="ticket_design_posted" value="1">
      <strong style="font-size:14px">The ticket <small style="font-weight:400;color:#8a9a9c">(what an attendee shows at the door)</small></strong>
      <p style="font-size:12px;color:#8a9a9c;margin:6px 0 12px">
        {% if design.customised %}This event has its own ticket design.{% else %}Using the
        standard design. Change anything below and only this event's tickets change.{% endif %}
      </p>

      {# `min-width:0` on the CHILD, not only `minmax(0,…)` on the track. A grid item's
         default `min-width:auto` is its content's minimum, and the form's inputs are
         `width:100%` of that — so the left column grew past its track and slid under the
         preview. The track sizing alone does not prevent it. #}
      <div class="tk-des">
        <div style="min-width:0">
          <div class="row">
            <label>Accent colour
              {# Two inputs, one value: the picker is unusable for typing a brand hex and the
                 text box is unusable for choosing one by eye. They are kept in step in
                 Alpine, and only `ticket_accent` is submitted. #}
              <span style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center">
                <input type="color" x-model="accent" aria-label="Accent colour picker"
                       style="width:44px;height:38px;padding:2px;flex:none;cursor:pointer">
                <input type="text" name="ticket_accent" x-model="accent" maxlength="7"
                       placeholder="#10292C" spellcheck="false"
                       style="font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace)">
              </span>
            </label>
            <label>Card
              <select name="ticket_theme" x-model="theme">
                <option value="dark">Dark card</option>
                <option value="light">Light card</option>
              </select>
            </label>
          </div>

          {# ── THE ARTWORK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
             This used to be a text box you typed a path into, and whatever was at that path
             got dropped into the ticket's band by CSS with one hard-coded focal point —
             `object-position:50% 32%`, chosen once against the average poster. On the events
             it was wrong for it cut somebody's face in half, and there was nothing an
             organiser could do about it from here.

             Now the frame is the band. What is inside it is what prints, at the ticket's own
             gradient and with the ticket's own title over it, so the one mistake this thing
             exists to prevent — putting the subject in the bottom third, where the type block
             lands — is visible before saving rather than after printing.

             The browser posts NUMBERS. The crop, the turn and the three adjustments go to the
             server as a small JSON recipe and AfricaGates\Services\TicketArtwork does the
             actual cutting with Intervention. A canvas export would be fewer moving parts and
             it is deliberately not what happens: it would walk around the upload hardening,
             and it would throw away the original, so the second edit would be cropping a crop. #}
          {% if artwork_missing is not empty %}
            <label>Ticket image <small>(blank = the event's cover image)</small>
              <input type="text" name="ticket_image" x-model="imageField"
                     placeholder="/uploads/ticket-art.jpg or https://…"></label>
            <p style="font-size:12px;color:#8a9a9c;margin:-2px 0 12px">
              The crop editor needs one more migration —
              <code>{{ artwork_missing|join('</code>, <code>')|raw }}</code>. Run
              <strong>/__setup/migrate</strong> and it appears here. Until then this is an
              address box, exactly as before.
            </p>
          {% else %}
          <span style="display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a9a9c;margin:2px 0 7px">The band at the top of the ticket</span>
          <div class="tka">
            {# The values the server reads. `ticket_image_edit` is rebuilt on every change, so
               whatever the frame is showing when Save is pressed is what gets cut. #}
            <input type="hidden" name="ticket_image_edit" :value="artJson()">
            <input type="hidden" name="ticket_artwork_clear" :value="art.gone ? '1' : ''">

            <template x-if="art.src">
              <div class="tka__frame" x-ref="tkaFrame" tabindex="0" role="group"
                   aria-label="Ticket artwork — drag to move, arrow keys to nudge, scroll to zoom"
                   @pointerdown="artGrab($event)" @keydown="artKey($event)"
                   @wheel.prevent="artZoom($event.deltaY < 0 ? 0.12 : -0.12)">
                <div class="tka__stage" :style="artStage()">
                  <img class="tka__img" :src="art.src" :style="artImg()" alt=""
                       aria-hidden="true" draggable="false" @load="artLoaded($event)">
                </div>
                {# The ticket's own wash, at the ticket's own stops — see the note on
                   .tk__scrim in templates/pages/events/ticket.twig for where each comes from. #}
                <span class="tka__wash" aria-hidden="true"
                      :style="'background:linear-gradient(to top,' + accent + 'F7 0%,' + accent + 'F2 48%,' + accent + 'B0 62%,' + accent + '00 78%)'"></span>
                <div class="tka__over" aria-hidden="true" :style="'color:' + ink()">
                  <span class="tka__overk" x-text="[artDay(), venue].filter(Boolean).join(' · ') || 'Admit one'"></span>
                  <span class="tka__overt" x-text="title || 'Your event'"></span>
                </div>
                <span class="tka__guide" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </div>
            </template>

            {# ── ONE FILE INPUT, AND IT NEVER MOVES ───────────────────────
               It sits outside both branches below and is reached by `for=`. Inside an
               `x-if` it would be the same control on screen and a different element in the
               DOM: choosing a picture sets `art.src`, which flips the branch, which destroys
               the input — taking the chosen file with it. The form then posted no file at
               all, the save looked like it worked, and nothing arrived. #}
            <input class="tka__file" type="file" id="tka-file" name="ticket_artwork"
                   accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp,image/gif" x-ref="tkaFile"
                   @change="artFile($event.target.files[0])">

            <template x-if="!art.src">
              <label class="tka__drop" for="tka-file" :class="art.over ? 'is-over' : ''"
                     @dragover.prevent="art.over = true" @dragleave="art.over = false"
                     @drop.prevent="art.over = false; artDrop($event)">
                <strong>Add the ticket artwork</strong>
                <span>Drop a picture here, or choose one. JPEG, PNG or WebP, at least 300px on
                      the short side.</span>
              </label>
            </template>

            <template x-if="art.src">
              <div class="tka__tools">
                {# The same input as the drop zone — see the note above it. A `label for=` is
                   also the one way to open a file picker from the keyboard. #}
                <label class="tka__btn" for="tka-file">Replace</label>
                <button type="button" class="tka__btn" @click="artTurn(-90)"
                        aria-label="Turn a quarter turn anticlockwise" title="Turn anticlockwise">↺</button>
                <button type="button" class="tka__btn" @click="artTurn(90)"
                        aria-label="Turn a quarter turn clockwise" title="Turn clockwise">↻</button>
                <button type="button" class="tka__btn" @click="artFlip('h')"
                        :aria-pressed="art.flip === 'h' ? 'true' : 'false'"
                        aria-label="Mirror left to right" title="Mirror left to right">⇋</button>
                <button type="button" class="tka__btn" @click="artFlip('v')"
                        :aria-pressed="art.flip === 'v' ? 'true' : 'false'"
                        aria-label="Mirror top to bottom" title="Mirror top to bottom">⇅</button>
                <button type="button" class="tka__btn" @click="art.greyscale = !art.greyscale"
                        :aria-pressed="art.greyscale ? 'true' : 'false'">Black &amp; white</button>
                <button type="button" class="tka__btn" @click="artReset()"
                        :disabled="artUntouched()">Reset</button>
                <button type="button" class="tka__btn tka__btn--warn" @click="artRemove()">Remove</button>
              </div>
            </template>

            <template x-if="art.src">
              <div class="tka__grid">
                <label class="tka__slide"><span>Zoom</span>
                  <input type="range" min="1" max="4" step="0.02" x-model.number="art.zoom"
                         @input="artClamp()">
                  <span class="tka__val" x-text="art.zoom.toFixed(2) + '×'"></span></label>
                <label class="tka__slide"><span>Brightness</span>
                  <input type="range" min="-100" max="100" step="1" x-model.number="art.brightness">
                  <span class="tka__val" x-text="artSigned(art.brightness)"></span></label>
                <label class="tka__slide"><span>Contrast</span>
                  <input type="range" min="-100" max="100" step="1" x-model.number="art.contrast">
                  <span class="tka__val" x-text="artSigned(art.contrast)"></span></label>
              </div>
            </template>

            {# The filter the frame is looking through, and the one the server will apply.
               feComponentTransfer's `linear` is ADDITIVE, which is what GD's brightness is;
               CSS `brightness()` is multiplicative and would preview a different picture from
               the one that prints. The matrix uses GD's own greyscale weights (.299 .587 .114)
               rather than CSS `grayscale()`'s Rec.709 ones, for the same reason. Contrast is
               the one that maps cleanly — CSS `contrast(k)` is exactly GD's
               `(c - .5) * k + .5`, so it is applied as a plain CSS function in artFilter(). #}
            <svg class="tka__defs" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <filter id="tka-adj" color-interpolation-filters="sRGB">
                <feColorMatrix type="matrix" :values="artMatrix()"></feColorMatrix>
                <feComponentTransfer>
                  <feFuncR type="linear" slope="1" :intercept="art.brightness / 100"></feFuncR>
                  <feFuncG type="linear" slope="1" :intercept="art.brightness / 100"></feFuncG>
                  <feFuncB type="linear" slope="1" :intercept="art.brightness / 100"></feFuncB>
                </feComponentTransfer>
              </filter>
            </svg>

            <p style="font-size:12px;color:#8a9a9c;margin:10px 0 0">
              Drag the picture to move it, scroll or use Zoom to fill the frame. The original
              is kept, so every change is cut from it fresh — you can come back and re-frame
              this next year without the picture getting any softer.
            </p>

            {# Folded away. An address is the escape hatch for artwork that lives somewhere
               else, and it is the wrong first thing to offer somebody holding a JPEG. #}
            <details style="margin-top:10px">
              <summary style="font-size:13px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;color:#5a6d6f">Use a picture that is already online</summary>
              <label style="margin-top:8px">Address of the image
                <input type="text" name="ticket_image" x-model="imageField"
                       placeholder="/uploads/ticket-art.jpg or https://…"></label>
              <p style="font-size:12px;color:#8a9a9c;margin:-2px 0 4px">
                Shown as-is: a picture we did not receive as a file cannot be cropped here, so
                it is fitted to the band the old way. Typing an address replaces any artwork
                above — leave this alone if you are using the frame.
              </p>
            </details>
          </div>
          {% endif %}

          <label>Line on the stub <small>(printed — “Doors 5pm · Black tie”)</small>
            <input type="text" name="ticket_note" x-model="note" maxlength="160"></label>

          <fieldset style="border:1px solid var(--cn-line-card);border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;margin:10px 0 0">
            <legend style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a9a9c;padding:0 4px">Show on the ticket</legend>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 16px;margin-top:4px">
              {% for key, label in design_rows %}
                <label style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:13px;margin:0">
                  <input type="checkbox" name="ticket_rows[]" value="{{ key }}"
                         {% if key in design.rows %}checked{% endif %}
                         style="width:auto;flex:none;margin:0">
                  <span>{{ label }}</span>
                </label>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
            <p style="font-size:12px;color:#8a9a9c;margin:10px 0 0">
              The holder's name, the ticket type and the reference always show — a ticket
              without them is not a ticket. A row with nothing in it is skipped, so ticking
              “Seat” costs nothing on events that do not use one.
            </p>
          </fieldset>

          <label style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:12px">
            <input type="checkbox" name="ticket_show_qr" value="1" x-model="showQr"
                   style="width:auto;flex:none;margin:0">
            <span>Print a QR code on the ticket</span>
          </label>
          <p style="font-size:12px;color:#8a9a9c;margin:4px 0 0">
            Leave this on unless your door checks names against a printed list. Typing nine
            characters per attendee is what makes a queue stationary — at three hundred people
            it is about twenty minutes of queue that need not exist. The code is printed
            either way, so a phone with a dead battery is never locked out.
          </p>
        </div>

        {# ── the preview ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
           Not the real template — it is a sketch at a quarter of the detail, and it exists
           so a colour choice can be judged before saving. The QR is a placeholder grid
           rather than a real symbol: generating one per keystroke would be a request per
           keystroke, and what is being judged here is the colour, not the code. #}
        <div style="min-width:0">
          <span style="display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a9a9c;margin-bottom:7px">Preview</span>
          <div :class="theme === 'dark' ? 'tkp tkp--dark' : 'tkp'">
            <div class="tkp__head" :style="'background:' + accent + ';color:' + ink()">
              {# Cropped artwork wins over a pasted address, because that is the order the
                 server resolves them in — a preview that disagreed would be worse than none. #}
              <template x-if="art.src">
                <span class="tkp__art" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="tkp__stage" :style="artStage()">
                    <img class="tka__img" :src="art.src" :style="artImg()" alt="" draggable="false">
                  </span>
                </span>
              </template>
              <template x-if="!art.src && shot()">
                <img class="tkp__shot" :src="shot()" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
              </template>
              <template x-if="art.src || shot()">
                <span class="tkp__scrim" :style="'background:linear-gradient(180deg,' + accent + 'F0,' + accent + 'FC)'"></span>
              </template>
              <div class="tkp__headin">
                <span class="tkp__eyebrow">Admit one</span>
                <strong class="tkp__title" x-text="title || 'Your event'"></strong>
                <span class="tkp__when" x-text="[when, venue].filter(Boolean).join(' · ')"></span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="tkp__tear"><i></i></div>
            <div class="tkp__stub">
              <template x-if="showQr"><span class="tkp__qr" aria-hidden="true"></span></template>
              <span class="tkp__code">ABCD-2468</span>
              <template x-if="note"><span class="tkp__note" x-text="note"></span></template>
            </div>
            <div class="tkp__rows">
              <span>Ada Obi</span><span>Ceremony</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    </section>
